                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Gravity and orbital mechanics got me hooked in. And boy it's implemented very well!\r\n\r\nThe game's artwork is distinctive and grew on me as I played more. The story is told in fragments and in a flashback style manner. The dialogues and the setting didn't seem to match up completely but I'm just nitpicking at this point.\r\n\r\nThe orbital mechanics are splendid and will keep you hooked! You still get to learn new techniques more than halfway through the game, yet it doesn't feel very short. Mastering your techniques is a whole other thing altogether. Some of the achievements will require you to play the game a second time but I feel this doesn't have very good replayability. \r\n\r\nA great game with minimalistic graphics and awesome physics! \r\n\r\n- 9/10",
